{title: 430 - Joy By and By}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]O there'll be joy when the [F]work [F7]is done,
[F7]Joy when the reapers [Eb/Bb]gather [Bb]home,
[Bb]Bringing the sheaves [Eb]at set of sun
[Bb]To the New [Gm]Jerusalem.

Refrain:
[Bb]Joy, joy, joy, there'll be [F]joy [Bb/F]by and [F7]by,
[F7]Joy, joy, joy, [Cm]where the [Bb]joys [F7]never [Bb]die;
[Bb]Joy, [Gm]joy, joy, [Bb/F]for the [Eb]day draweth nigh
[Bb/F]When the workers [F7]gather [Bb]home.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Sweet are the songs that we [F]hope [F7]to sing,
[F7]Grateful the thanks our [Eb/Bb]hearts [Bb]shall bring,
[Bb]Praising forever [Eb]Christ our King
[Bb]In the New [Gm]Jerusalem.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Pure are the joys that await [F7]us there,
[F7]Many the golden [Eb/Bb]mansions [Bb]fair;
[Bb]Jesus Himself [Eb]doth them prepare,
[Bb]In the New [Gm]Jerusalem.
